## §3 Data flow

The schema is a **validator at two write chokepoints and a shape contract at one read
boundary**. It is never on a mutating egress path — SAKG has none (§3.3.1).

```
  PAEOS goal reaches L16 and seals
            │
            ▼
  L15 → runtime/emission/outbox.py            [I-OUTBOX, PAEOS side]
            │  append-only outbox record
            ▼
  sakg/extract.py  PAEOS artifact → typed node dicts     [I-EXTRACT]
            │  L06 matrix→TradeOff · L04 candidates→Option (incl. rejected)
            │  L08 set→Component · L11 contract→Constraint
            │  decision-graph→Decision · scar-graph→Scar · CAS hashes→EvidenceRef
            ▼
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║ CHOKEPOINT 1 — INGEST ADMISSION            [I-INGEST]        ║
  ║ validate(node, envelope.schema.json)                         ║
  ║   pass → write at status=candidate, namespace=producer       ║
  ║   fail → explicit gap record; NEVER a silent drop            ║
  ║ forced by schema: status=candidate ⟹ no promotion facet (R9) ║
  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
            │
            ▼
  sakg/store.py  append-only node + edge persistence      [I-STORE]
            │
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║ CHOKEPOINT 2 — EVERY WRITE                 [I-STORE]         ║
  ║ each status change appends a NEW document that must re-      ║
  ║ validate. Nothing is edited in place; nothing is removed.    ║
  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
            │
            ├── Truth Maintenance recomputes confidence
            │     → new sakg.confidence_derivation, recompute_seq += 1
            │     → propagates along derived_from / supports edges  (Δ6, L2/IT-05)
            │
            ▼
  sakg/project.py  budget-bounded projection              [I-PROJ]
            │  node_summary  ← envelope.summary   (≤ 280 chars — the Ω3 unit)
            │  score, why    ← traversal, not envelope
            ▼
  Consumer, tagged provenance=sakg · trust=untrusted · tier=SUMMARY|INDEX
```

**Read-boundary consequence.** `summary`'s 280-character cap is not cosmetic: it is the
quantum the §5.1 budget arithmetic counts. If the cap moved, every `max_tokens` guarantee
downstream would move with it. This is precisely why it is frozen here, upstream of
`F-PROJ` and `F-BUDGET-FIX`, and why the corpus carries both a 280-ASCII and a
280-multibyte boundary fixture (see **GAP-5**).

**Cold start (§7).** An empty graph is a valid state. The schema constrains documents, not
cardinality — there is no `minItems` anywhere that a zero-node corpus could violate. This
is what lets `test_empty_graph_returns_empty_not_error.py` pass by construction.

