## §14 Design-time verification (throwaway prototype, not a deliverable)

The mechanism in §2.4 is the load-bearing and least obvious part of this design, so it was
**prototyped and executed** in a scratch directory (`/tmp`, outside both the repo and this
session's write-capability) before being frozen here. No repository file was produced by
that run; it exists only to falsify the design while changing it is still cheap.

What was executed, against `jsonschema 4.26.0` / `Draft202012Validator`:

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `check_schema` on the full §2 schema (all 14 properties, all 20 `allOf` branches, all 5 reserved-facet `$defs`) | **passes** — the design is legal draft 2020-12 |
| `V01`, `V02`, `V12`, `V13` (maximal, minimal, refuted, EvidenceRef) | **all validate clean** — the four structurally hardest valid shapes |
| All 13 invalid fixtures of §6.3 | **all rejected** |
| Declared failure locus (pointer + keyword) for each of the 13 | **all confirmed as emitted** |
| ULID/URI/timestamp patterns of §2.2 | confirmed: 26-char pinned ULIDs match; the character class equals the Crockford alphabet exactly (`I/L/O/U` rejected); hyphenated `ProjectRef` matches; a timestamp without millisecond precision is rejected |

Two design defects were found and are already corrected above: the `X09` base was cascading
into three loci (fixed by rebasing onto `V01`), and the `X05` root pointer was written
ambiguously (fixed to `""`).

This is **design evidence, not `accept` evidence.** The four `accept` commands of §8 remain
unrun and belong to VERIFY; a prototype in `/tmp` proves the design is realisable, not that
the deliverables exist.

